{{!-- v3 nav rail (add-pc-sheet-v3 §8.3/§8.4/§8.6) — forked from `parts/navigation.hbs`.

      WHY A FORK, AND WHY IT IS STILL A SHELL (D5)
      ----------------------------------------------
      The v2 rail (`parts/navigation.hbs`, unchanged and still what every non-opted-in actor
      renders) is one `{{#each tabs}}` loop. This file is the same loop, run twice against the
      SAME `tabs` collection: once for the five content tabs, once for the administrative one
      (Ajustes/Settings), so the second group can sit in its own visually-demoted cluster (§8.4) at
      the end of the rail. Nothing here is a row renderer — each `<div data-action="tab" …>` is
      authored identically to v2's, same attributes, same classes off `tab.cssClass` — it is layout
      ONLY, split into two containers instead of one.

      THE WIKI LINK (reorganize-mage-sheet-v3)
      -----------------------------------------
      Unlike the rest of this file, the wiki `<a>` at the bottom is DELIBERATELY NOT identical to
      v2's any more: it points at this fork's own wiki
      (`https://github.com/LudoBermejoES/Foundry_WoD20/wiki`), the repo this system is actually
      deployed from, instead of upstream's (`github.com/JohanFalt/Foundry_WoD20`). This is the ONE
      link repointed — `parts/navigation.hbs` (v2's rail), `module/ui/settings-sidebar.js`,
      `module/migration.js` and `wod.js` all keep upstream's URL on purpose, because those deep-link
      to specific pages (`Feature:-API`, `PC-Actor`, `Changelog#fix-of-v72`) that are not guaranteed
      to exist on the fork's wiki — only the fork's own wiki ROOT is a safe target.

      WHERE EFFECTS WENT (§8.3)
      --------------------------
      Effects has NO icon of its own here any more — `tab.id === "effects"` cannot occur in the
      `{{#each tabs}}` below at all, because `PCActorSheetV3`'s own `tabs` field (the one this
      partial iterates) declares no `effects` entry. Its content now renders as a SUB-TAB inside
      Ajustes: `templates/actor/parts/settings.hbs`'s existing `<nav class="sheet-setting-tabs">` +
      sibling `.tab[data-group="settings"]` machinery, gated on `effectsinsettings`, one nav link
      and one body div (`templates/actor/v3/effects_body.hbs`) added to that SHARED template — no
      fork of it, no duplicated rows (D5). See `settings.hbs` and `PCActorSheet#effectsInSettings`.

      THE BADGE (§8.6)
      -----------------
      `tab.count`, when present, is a plain item count computed in
      `PCActorSheetV3#_prepareContext` — the ROOT context, not a part preparer. This part (`tabs`)
      has no `case` in `_preparePartContext` at all, so it is the one part on either sheet that
      never runs a preparer of its own; a count set anywhere else would never reach here. Rendered
      as `aria-hidden`, because a bare number floating beside an icon announces nothing useful to
      assistive technology on its own — the tab's own `title` already names what is inside it.
      `tabs.settings.count` is now the Effects count too (§8.3: there is no `tabs.effects` any more
      for it to sit beside), so the Ajustes icon below is where a GM sees "something in there". --}}
<div class="tabs-container">
    <nav class="sheet-tabs tabs v3-tabs" data-group="primary">
        {{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/navigation_lock.hbs"}}

        {{#each tabs as |tab|}}
            {{#unless (eq tab.id "settings")}}
                <div class="{{tab.cssClass}}" data-action="tab" data-group="{{tab.group}}" data-tab="{{tab.id}}" title="{{localize tab.title}}">
                    <div class="navicon">
                        {{{tab.icon}}}
                    </div>
                    {{#if tab.count}}
                        <span class="v3-navbadge" aria-hidden="true">{{tab.count}}</span>
                    {{/if}}
                </div>
            {{/unless}}
        {{/each}}

        <div class="v3-navadmin">
            {{#each tabs as |tab|}}
                {{#if (eq tab.id "settings")}}
                    <div class="{{tab.cssClass}} v3-navadmin-item" data-action="tab" data-group="{{tab.group}}" data-tab="{{tab.id}}" title="{{localize tab.title}}">
                        <div class="navicon">
                            {{{tab.icon}}}
                        </div>
                        {{#if tab.count}}
                            <span class="v3-navbadge" aria-hidden="true">{{tab.count}}</span>
                        {{/if}}
                    </div>
                {{/if}}
            {{/each}}
        </div>

        <a href="https://github.com/LudoBermejoES/Foundry_WoD20/wiki" target="_blank" class="item" title="Wiki">{{> (dtSvgDie 'dice' actor.type actor.system.settings.variantsheet)}}</a>
    </nav>
</div>
